LONG5.push(
 {t:'Ruth Asawa: Shapes from Wire',k:'Article',p:[
  'Ruth Asawa was born in California in 1926. Her family were farmers, and as a girl she drew pictures in the dirt with her feet while she worked in the fields.',
  'During World War II, Ruth and her family were forced to leave their home and live in camps with other Japanese Americans. In the camps, she met artists who taught her to draw.',
  'Later, on a trip to Mexico, Ruth watched people weave baskets from wire. She began to crochet wire into looping shapes that looked like floating clouds or sea creatures.',
  'Many people at first said her sculptures were "just crafts." Ruth kept working anyway. Today, her art hangs in major museums, and San Francisco named a school after her.',
  'Ruth also believed every child should be able to make art. She helped start art programs in public schools so students could learn from real artists.'],
  q:[['mc','What is the main idea of the article?','Ruth Asawa overcame hard times to become an important artist who also helped children make art.',['Wire is easy to bend.','Mexico is known for baskets.','Museums only show paintings.'],'What is the whole article about?','It tells <b>how Ruth Asawa became an artist and helped others</b>.'],
     ['ab','<b>Part A:</b> Which word best describes Ruth Asawa?','determined',['careless','jealous','shy'],'<b>Part B:</b> Which sentence best supports your answer in Part A?','Ruth kept working anyway.',['Ruth Asawa was born in California in 1926.','Her family were farmers.','She began to crochet wire into looping shapes.'],'What did she do when people doubted her?','She did not give up: <b>Ruth kept working anyway</b>.'],
     ['two','Which <b>two</b> events helped Ruth learn about art?',['She met artists in the camps who taught her to draw.','She watched people weave baskets from wire in Mexico.'],['She worked in the fields.','San Francisco named a school after her.','People called her art "just crafts."'],'Look for where she learned.','She learned from <b>artists in the camps</b> and from <b>wire basket weavers</b>.'],
     ['hl','Tap the sentence that shows how Ruth helped other children.','She helped start art programs in public schools','Look at the last paragraph.','<b>She helped start art programs in public schools</b>.'],
     ['mc','How is the article mostly organized?','in time order, from Ruth\'s childhood to later in her life',['as a list of opinions','as a comparison of two artists','as steps to make a sculpture'],'Look at the beginning of each paragraph.','It follows her life <b>in time order</b>.']]},
 {t:'The Stormy Crossing (a story told by Leo)',k:'Story',p:[
  'My little sister, Gaby, had never been on a boat, so when Dad said we would take the ferry to the island, she bounced all the way to the dock.',
  'Halfway across, the sky turned the color of an old bruise. Waves slapped the side of the ferry, and Gaby grabbed my arm so hard it hurt.',
  'I was scared too, but I remembered what Grandpa always said: "When the sea gets loud, make your voice calm." So I told Gaby stories about the dolphins we might see.',
  'By the time the island appeared through the rain, Gaby was laughing at my silly dolphin voices. Dad winked at me.',
  'That night, Gaby told Mom that the storm was the best part of the trip. I didn\'t tell her how fast my own heart had been beating.'],
  q:[['mc','Who is telling the story?','Leo, Gaby\'s older brother',['Gaby','Dad','Grandpa'],'Look at the title and the word "my".','The narrator is <b>Leo</b>, telling it in first person.'],
     ['ab','<b>Part A:</b> How does Leo feel during the storm?','scared, but he stays calm for his sister',['bored','angry at Dad','excited the whole time'],'<b>Part B:</b> Which sentence best supports your answer in Part A?','I was scared too, but I remembered what Grandpa always said: "When the sea gets loud, make your voice calm."',['My little sister, Gaby, had never been on a boat.','Dad winked at me.','By the time the island appeared through the rain, Gaby was laughing.'],'Look at paragraph 3.','He was <b>scared too</b> but used Grandpa\'s advice to stay calm.'],
     ['mc','What does the phrase "the color of an old bruise" describe?','a dark, purple-gray stormy sky',['Gaby\'s arm','the ferry','a sunset'],'What turned that color?','It describes the <b>dark stormy sky</b>.'],
     ['hl','Tap the sentence that shows Leo hid his own fear from Gaby.','I didn\'t tell her how fast my own heart had been beating.','Look at the last paragraph.','<b>He didn\'t tell her</b> how scared he had been.'],
     ['mc','How would the story be different if Gaby told it?','Readers might not know Leo was scared.',['There would be no storm.','Dad would be the main character.','The story would be about dolphins only.'],'What does only Leo know?','Only Leo knows his heart was racing, so <b>Gaby might not know he was scared</b>.']]}
);
LONG5Q.push(...LONG5.slice(L5n).flatMap((P,k)=>P.q.map((_,qi)=>[L5n+k,qi])));
LISTEN5.push(
 {t:'How Volcanoes Form Islands',txt:'Did you know that the Hawaiian Islands were built by volcanoes? Deep under the Pacific Ocean, there is a hot spot where melted rock rises from inside Earth. Each time a volcano erupts there, lava cools and hardens into new rock. Over hundreds of thousands of years, the rock piles higher and higher until it rises above the water as an island. Because the ocean floor slowly moves, new islands form in a line, one after another. The youngest island, the Big Island, still has active volcanoes today.',
  q:[['What is the speaker\'s main point?','Volcanoes over a hot spot built the Hawaiian Islands over a very long time.',['Hawaii is a nice place to visit.','All islands are made of sand.','Volcanoes only happen on land.'],'Listen for the big idea in the first sentence.','Volcanoes <b>built the islands</b> over a long time.'],
     ['Why do the islands form in a line?','The ocean floor slowly moves over the hot spot.',['Someone planned them that way.','The wind blows them.','Lava flows in one direction only.'],'Listen for the word "because".','<b>The ocean floor moves</b>, so new islands form in a line.'],
     ['Which detail supports the idea that the Big Island is the youngest?','It still has active volcanoes.',['It is the biggest.','It has the most people.','It is the farthest north.'],'Listen to the last sentence.','Its volcanoes are <b>still active</b>.']]},
 {t:'Class President Debate',txt:'Good afternoon. My name is Aisha, and I believe our school needs more water fountains. Right now, there are only two fountains for four hundred students, so lines at recess are long, and many kids go back to class thirsty. Last month, I counted the line every day: it averaged twelve students. If I am elected, I will ask the principal to add two refill stations, which also cut down on plastic bottles. A healthy school is a hydrated school. Thank you.',
  q:[['What is Aisha\'s main claim?','The school needs more water fountains.',['Recess should be longer.','Plastic bottles are good.','The principal is wrong.'],'Listen for "I believe".','She believes the school <b>needs more water fountains</b>.'],
     ['Which evidence does Aisha give?','She counted an average of twelve students in line each day.',['She says water tastes good.','She says her friends agree.','She says fountains are blue.'],'Listen for numbers.','She <b>counted the line every day</b>: about twelve students.'],
     ['Which reason does Aisha give for refill stations besides less waiting?','They cut down on plastic bottles.',['They are cheaper than pizza.','They play music.','They are taller.'],'Listen for "which also".','Refill stations <b>cut down on plastic bottles</b>.']]},
 {t:'The Story of the Golden Spike',txt:'On May tenth, eighteen sixty-nine, two railroad companies met at Promontory Summit in Utah. The Central Pacific had built east from California, and the Union Pacific had built west from Nebraska. Workers, including thousands of Chinese and Irish immigrants, had laid tracks across mountains and deserts. A golden spike was tapped into the final tie, and a telegraph message of one word, "Done," was sent across the country. Now a trip from coast to coast took about a week instead of months.',
  q:[['Where did the two railroads meet?','Promontory Summit, Utah',['San Francisco, California','Omaha, Nebraska','New York City'],'Listen to the first sentence.','They met at <b>Promontory Summit, Utah</b>.'],
     ['Who did much of the work building the railroad?','thousands of Chinese and Irish immigrants',['only soldiers','only children','the president'],'Listen for who laid the tracks.','<b>Chinese and Irish immigrants</b> did much of the work.'],
     ['How did the railroad change travel?','A coast-to-coast trip took about a week instead of months.',['Travel became slower.','People stopped traveling.','Only mail could travel.'],'Listen to the last sentence.','The trip took <b>about a week instead of months</b>.']]}
);
